  "description": "Manufacturer may substitute components with components of equal or greater performance level\n\nExperience the city like never before with the Nishiki Cordova—where contemporary design meets practicality. Whether you use your bike to commute, explore, work out, or all of the above, Cordova's capability and versatility allow it to fit seamlessly into your day-to-day, no matter what’s on the agenda. Its upright riding position ensures comfort as you navigate busy streets, while the rugged construction gets you from downtown to uptown without a hitch. Equipped with tough 27.5-inch wheels, the Cordova can handle the roughest of pavements, providing stability and control on your journey.\n\nFeatures:\n\nHybrid commuter bike capable of road, path and pavement rides\n\nLightweight 6061 aluminum frame with internal cables, double water bottle mounts, tapered head tube and replaceable derailleur hanger\n\nThis lightweight frame is responsive to pedal and easy to carry up and down stairs\n\nThis hybrid combines great comfort features with an upgraded road bike-style drivetrain that's lighter and better geared for performance\n\nLightweight 6061 aluminum urban fork\n\nMechanical disc brakes for sure stopping power; thesebrakes perform well in any weather, let you slow down or stop faster, and require less effort to activate than rim brakes\n\nShimano 12-32T, 1 x 8 speed drivetrain gearing makes it easy to ride on flat or hilly terrain\n\nSamox Forged, 42T crankset\n\nThis bike upright geometry puts you in the perfect position to see the world around you\n\nBike weighs approximately 33lbs",
